<newsitem itemid="251681" id="root" date="1996-12-12" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Premier half year shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Premier half year shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended October 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     15.1	  vs 12.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 5.0	   vs 4.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   159.1	 vs 100.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast earnings per share for the six months ended October ranging between 15.0 cents and 16.2 cents, with consensus at 15.6 cents.</p>
<p>Analysts ranged the half-year dividend between 4.8 and 5.4 cents, with consensus at 5.1 cents.  </p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   258.4	 vs 183.9</p>
<p>    Tax			 72.8	  vs 73.6</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   45.9	  vs 77.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		  8,095.9     vs 7,788.8</p>
<p>Full name: Premier Group Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     24.9 profit vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: - Directors said Premier would award capitalisation shares to shareholders registered on January 3, 1997 in the ratio that 5.0 cents per share multiplied by 1.075 bears to the issue price. This price was defined as the weighted average traded price of shares for the four days ending January 31.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
